# A root successor: a's successor, in a context of its own, sends C back to a (Succ at the root, Pred into it).
# Expect: consistent; A ⊑ C.
@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty . :A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] .
:B rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty [ owl:inverseOf :r ] ; owl:allValuesFrom :C ] .
:C owl:disjointWith :D .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual , :A .

